    "institutions_today": [],
    "paragraph": "CAROLINA introduces a deep causal inference framework for discrete choice modeling that isolates causal effects from observed and unobserved confounders in travel behavior analysis. Archaeological salvage excavations at the open-air Howard Creek site in Southeast Queensland recovered 11,990 lithic artifacts, establishing occupation of the sub-coastal region over the last 2,000 years. Finally, a Hanoi case study implemented a time-aware flood-routing engine within GraphHopper that updates dynamically using a rolling two-hour hydrodynamic forecast to close inundated roads based on vehicle-specific depth limits.",
